 "sarf": [
  {
   "type": "basic",
   "front": "What is the difference between a <bdi>وَزْن</bdi> and a <bdi>صِيغَة</bdi>?",
   "back": "The <bdi>وَزْن</bdi> is the pattern, on <bdi>ف ع ل</bdi>; the <bdi>صِيغَة</bdi> is the actual entry in the table",
   "tags": [
    "sarf",
    "wazn",
    "contrast"
   ],
   "tier": 1,
   "id": "sarf-248",
   "session": "oct27",
   "source": "IOK Arabic — Ṣarf: thulāthī mazīd fīh and rubāʿī — class notes 2026-10-27"
  },
  {
   "type": "basic",
   "front": "In <bdi>بَاب التَّفَعُّل</bdi> and <bdi>بَاب التَّفَاعُل</bdi>, which <bdi>مُضَارِع</bdi> forms can drop a <bdi>تَاء</bdi>?",
   "back": "Those that begin with <bdi>تَـ</bdi>: the two <bdi>تَاء</bdi>s can become one, so <bdi>تَتَقَبَّلُ</bdi> becomes <bdi>تَقَبَّلُ</bdi>, as in <bdi>تَنَزَّلُ المَلَائِكَةُ</bdi> (97:4). The <bdi>يَـ</bdi> forms, like <bdi>يَتَقَبَّلُ</bdi>, keep both letters.",
   "tags": [
    "sarf",
    "mazid",
    "tafaul"
   ],
   "tier": 1,
   "id": "sarf-249",
   "session": "oct27",
   "source": "IOK Arabic — Ṣarf: thulāthī mazīd fīh and rubāʿī — class notes 2026-10-27"
  },
  {
   "type": "basic",
   "front": "In <bdi>بَاب التَّفَعُّل</bdi> and <bdi>بَاب التَّفَاعُل</bdi>, what happens to the <bdi>تَاء</bdi> when the <bdi>فَاء</bdi> of the verb is a letter like <bdi>ز</bdi> or <bdi>د</bdi>?",
   "back": "It merges into the <bdi>فَاء</bdi>, which is doubled. The word now starts with a sākin letter, so a <bdi>هَمْزَة الوَصْل</bdi> is added: <bdi>تَزَمَّلَ</bdi> becomes <bdi>اِزَّمَّلَ</bdi>. So <bdi>المُزَّمِّل</bdi> is <bdi>المُتَزَمِّل</bdi>, and <bdi>المُدَّثِّر</bdi> is <bdi>المُتَدَثِّر</bdi>.",
   "tags": [
    "sarf",
    "mazid",
    "tafaul"
   ],
   "tier": 1,
   "id": "sarf-250",
   "session": "oct27",
   "source": "IOK Arabic — Ṣarf: thulāthī mazīd fīh and rubāʿī — class notes 2026-10-27"
  },
  {
   "type": "basic",
   "front": "Why does <bdi>بَاب الاِنْفِعَال</bdi> have no <bdi>مَجْهُول</bdi>?",
   "back": "It's intransitive: it means undergoing an action, as in <bdi>اِنْكَسَرَ</bdi>, “it broke”. There's no object to become the subject.",
   "tags": [
    "sarf",
    "mazid",
    "infiaal"
   ],
   "tier": 1,
   "id": "sarf-251",
   "session": "oct27",
   "source": "IOK Arabic — Ṣarf: thulāthī mazīd fīh and rubāʿī — class notes 2026-10-27"
  },
  {
   "type": "basic",
   "front": "What are the two kinds of <bdi>رُبَاعِيّ</bdi> verb?",
   "back": "One repeats a pair of letters, like <bdi>زَلْزَلَ</bdi> and <bdi>دَمْدَمَ</bdi>; the other has four different letters, like <bdi>بَعْثَرَ</bdi>",
   "tags": [
    "sarf",
    "rubai"
   ],
   "tier": 1,
   "id": "sarf-252",
   "session": "oct27",
   "source": "IOK Arabic — Ṣarf: thulāthī mazīd fīh and rubāʿī — class notes 2026-10-27"
  },
  {
   "type": "basic",
   "front": "Which <bdi>بَاب</bdi> is the <bdi>رُبَاعِيّ مُجَرَّد</bdi>, and which <bdi>بَاب</bdi> of the <bdi>رُبَاعِيّ مَزِيد فِيه</bdi> comes up in class?",
   "back": "<bdi>بَاب الفَعْلَلَة</bdi> (<bdi>فَعْلَلَ</bdi>), and <bdi>بَاب التَّفَعْلُل</bdi> (<bdi>تَفَعْلَلَ</bdi>)",
   "tags": [
    "sarf",
    "rubai"
   ],
   "tier": 1,
   "id": "sarf-253",
   "session": "oct27",
   "source": "IOK Arabic — Ṣarf: thulāthī mazīd fīh and rubāʿī — class notes 2026-10-27"
